A secret definition in Docker Compose

## Properties

- \`name\` (\`ComposeString\`): Custom name for this secret.
- \`environment\` (\`ComposeString\`): Name of an environment variable from which to get the secret value.
- \`file\` (\`ComposeString\`): Path to a file containing the secret value.
- \`external\` (\`boolean | ComposeString | { name?: ComposeString }\`): Specifies that this secret already exists and was created outside of Compose.
- \`labels\` (\`Record<string, ComposeString | number | boolean | null> | Array<ComposeString>\`): Add metadata to the secret using labels.
- \`driver\` (\`ComposeString\`): Specify which secret driver should be used for this secret.
- \`driver_opts\` (\`Record<string, ComposeString | number>\`): Specify driver-specific options.
- \`template_driver\` (\`ComposeString\`): Driver to use for templating the secret's value.
