type: resource-type
title: Network
description: A network definition in Docker Compose
name: Network
lexicon: docker
resource_type: Docker::Compose::Network
---
A network definition in Docker Compose

## Properties

- \`name\` (\`ComposeString\`): Custom name for this network.
- \`driver\` (\`ComposeString\`): Specify which driver should be used for this network. Default is 'bridge'.
- \`driver_opts\` (\`Record<string, ComposeString | number>\`): Specify driver-specific options defined as key/value pairs.
- \`ipam\` (\`{ driver?: ComposeString; config?: Array<{ subnet?: ComposeString; ip_range?: ComposeString; gateway?: ComposeString; aux_addresses?: Record<string, ComposeString>; [key: \`x-\${string}\`]: unknown }>; options?: Record<string, ComposeString>; [key: \`x-\${string}\`]: unknown }\`): Custom IP Address Management configuration for this network.
- \`external\` (\`boolean | ComposeString | { name?: ComposeString; [key: \`x-\${string}\`]: unknown }\`): Specifies that this network already exists and was created outside of Compose.
- \`internal\` (\`boolean | ComposeString\`): Create an externally isolated network.
- \`enable_ipv4\` (\`boolean | ComposeString\`): Enable IPv4 networking.
- \`enable_ipv6\` (\`boolean | ComposeString\`): Enable IPv6 networking.
- \`attachable\` (\`boolean | ComposeString\`): If true, standalone containers can attach to this network.
- \`labels\` (\`Record<string, ComposeString | number | boolean | null> | Array<ComposeString>\`): Add metadata to the network using labels.
",
