A named volume definition in Docker Compose

## Properties

- \`name\` (\`ComposeString\`): Custom name for this volume.
- \`driver\` (\`ComposeString\`): Specify which volume driver should be used for this volume.
- \`driver_opts\` (\`Record<string, ComposeString | number>\`): Specify driver-specific options.
- \`external\` (\`boolean | ComposeString | { name?: ComposeString; [key: \`x-\${string}\`]: unknown }\`): Specifies that this volume already exists and was created outside of Compose.
- \`labels\` (\`Record<string, ComposeString | number | boolean | null> | Array<ComposeString>\`): Add metadata to the volume using labels.

## Governed by

- [DKRD002](/rules/DKRD002.md): Named volume is declared but not mounted by any service
